0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le01ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, that was another fantastic meal. Thanks V! You must be happy to be home!\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It's good to be home. Who knew that a busted washing machine would cause so much change to my house?  I also had no idea how exorbitant it would be either.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Let's hope nothing else falls apart. As it is, I'm still having my electrician and plumber come in next week to fix a few small problems.  V, I should have known this was going to be much more expensive than it appeared at first.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  It always is. I've decided to get someone in to strip the paint in the apartment. I also got the landlord to pay for it."}, {"time": "36500", "image": "engenn9le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Did you get him to check the electrical issues? I almost electrocuted myself when I unplugged that lamp from the socket last night.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Why did you unplug it?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It was  making a strange sound.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That lamp needs to be thrown out!\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh boy. So much needs to be done. My apartment needs refurbishing but I can't do it all right now. I know new furniture also needs to be bought and the walls need to be painted.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Surely we could get a couple of people to paint your place. We can help too."}, {"time": "65000", "image": "engenn9le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Your kitchen cupboards also need to be replaced.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: That will have to wait. I have to draw the line somewhere.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I think the best idea would be to just buy a whole new house! Renovations are too expensive to believe.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Can we watch basketball now?"}]}}], "_data": [], "id": 1, "type": "audio"}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "Being a landlord isn't always easy. When I bought that apartment building I had to have someone inspect the whole building from the basement to the top floor. Because there were cockroaches, I got an exterminator to spray each floor. Next I had an electrician rewire the building so as not to be unsafe. Then I had the fire department come to check everything."}], "_data": [], "id": 2, "type": "text"}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Troubles at Home", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I Should Have Known!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le01ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Need</span> + Passive Infinitive and <span class=\"italic\">Need</span>+ Verb + <span class=\"italic\">ing</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Need</span> + passive infinitive</span> and <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">need</span> + verb + <span class=\"italic\">ing</span></span> are two structures you use to talk about fixing problems. You use these structures to imply that we don't know who will fix the problem, or that the person fixing the problem is not the focus of the sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Subject + Need + Passive Infinitive</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> The lamp needs to be <span class=\"strong\">thrown</span> out!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make sure you know the past participle of the main verb, especially if it's an irregular verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Throw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Threw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Thrown\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Subject + Need + Verb + ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> My apartment needs refurbishing.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "That lamp <span class=\"strong\">needs to be thrown out</span>!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Oh boy. So much <span class=\"strong\">needs to be done</span>. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My apartment <span class=\"strong\">needs refurbishing</span> but I can't do it all right now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I know new furniture also <span class=\"strong\">needs to be bought</span> and the walls <span class=\"strong\">need to be painted</span>. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Your kitchen cupboards also <span class=\"strong\">need to be replaced</span>. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Causative with <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Get</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the causative with have and get to show that you want someone to do something for you.  You cause the person to do something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Causative Form with Have</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + agent + base form of the verb + object", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I had them install my washer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/><span class=\"underline\">Causative Form with Get</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">get</span> + agent + infinitive + object", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'll get you guys to help me paint the house from top to bottom.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>Notice that <span class=\"italic\">have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">get</span> can be used in any verb tense or form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I<span class=\"strong\">'m still having</span> my electrician and plumber <span class=\"strong\">come in</span> next week to fix a few small problems.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I<span class=\"strong\">'ve decided to get</span> someone in <span class=\"strong\">to strip</span> the paint in the apartment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I also <span class=\"strong\">got</span> the landlord <span class=\"strong\">to pay</span> for it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Did</span> you <span class=\"strong\">get</span> him <span class=\"strong\">to check</span> the electrical issues? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Surely we <span class=\"strong\">could get</span> a couple of people <span class=\"strong\">to paint</span> your place.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "busted", "type": "name"}, {"content": "damaged or destroyed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Who knew that a busted washing machine would cause so much change to my house? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear/use when things in the house don't work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "exorbitant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "excessive, extravagant or immoderate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I also had no idea how exorbitant it would be either.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fall apart", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to break into pieces", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's hope nothing else falls apart.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to electrocute", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get injured by electric shock", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I almost electrocuted myself when I unplugged that lamp from the socket last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to unplug", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to disconnect by removing a plug from an electrical connection", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why did you unplug it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "socket", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a device to connect electrically by circuit wires", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I unplugged that lamp from the socket last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to refurbish", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to clean, decorate, or renovate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My apartment needs refurbishing but I can't do it all right now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to draw the line", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to set a limit on what one is willing to do or accept", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example I have to draw the line somewhere.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9Le01ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">Made</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Under the Tuscan Sun</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify and write down the types of repairs they need to make.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell a friend about the movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell the friend what needed to be done in the house.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch and listen to a movie about household problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write what needs to be done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tell a friend about the movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things that needed to be done.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}